Protect the weak reference finalizer before duplicating the value, so
R_MakeWeakRefC() cannot lose its finalizer to the collector.

NewWeakRef() (src/main/memory.c) protects key, val, fin in that order,
and the val step allocates:

    PROTECT(key);
    PROTECT(val = MAYBE_REFERENCED(val) ? duplicate(val) : val);
    PROTECT(fin);

R_MakeWeakRefC() passes a freshly allocated RAWSXP as fin, so when val
is a referenced object the duplicate() can collect it; the weak
reference then stores a recycled node as its finalizer and
R_RunWeakRefFinalizer() later calls a stale pointer or tries to eval()
whatever reused the node ("attempt to apply non-function").

Protect fin before val.  In-tree callers all pass val = R_NilValue, so
only packages calling R_MakeWeakRefC() with a value are exposed; carried
here so the fuzz builds' R matches the fix under review.

Found by static analysis (argument rooting inference over src/), not by
a fuzz target.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #379, filed 2026-10-15.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/memory.c
+++ b/src/main/memory.c
@@ -1399,8 +1399,10 @@ static SEXP NewWeakRef(SEXP key, SEXP val, SEXP fin, Rboolean onexit)
     }
 
     PROTECT(key);
-    PROTECT(val = MAYBE_REFERENCED(val) ? duplicate(val) : val);
+    /* fin before val: R_MakeWeakRefC() passes a fresh finalizer object,
+       and duplicate(val) below can collect it */
     PROTECT(fin);
+    PROTECT(val = MAYBE_REFERENCED(val) ? duplicate(val) : val);
     w = allocVector(VECSXP, WEAKREF_SIZE);
     SET_TYPEOF(w, WEAKREFSXP);
     if (key != R_NilValue) {
